PORT=5000
# PORT=https://task-manegment-system-backend.onrender.com


Feature Implementation Specification: Personal Device Monitoring and Data Sync
1. Main Objective
Existing React Native application, Node.js/Express.js backend aur MongoDB database mein permission-based personal device monitoring functionality implement karo.

System mein do devices honge:

Device A: Admin phone, jahan se authorized device ka synchronized data view hoga.
Device B: Monitored personal phone, jo permitted device data collect karega, locally store karega aur server par synchronize karega.
Existing codebase, API structure, authentication, MongoDB models aur navigation ko reuse karo. Existing functionality ko break mat karo. Pehle current implementation inspect karo aur uske baad missing functionality add karo.

2. Device Registration and Pairing Flow
Device B par user apne account se login karega.
App device registration request backend ko bhejega.
Backend unique device ID, device name, platform, app version aur registration timestamp store karega.
Admin Device A se login karega.
Admin dashboard mein paired devices list hongi.
Device pairing secure, authenticated aur explicitly authorized honi chahiye.
Admin sirf apne account ke enrolled devices ka data access kar sakega.
Device unlink, account logout aur access revocation support karo.
3. Permission Management Flow
Device B par dedicated Permission Center screen implement karo.

Har module ke liye show karo:

Permission status
Feature availability
Last permission check
Enable instructions
Last successful collection timestamp
Error ya restriction details
Modules:

Notification access
Usage statistics access
Call history, if supported and authorized
Selected gallery media
Selected files and documents
Optional screen sharing
Permissions ko silently enable karne ki koshish mat karo. Required Android system settings, runtime permissions aur consent dialogs ka use karo.

Permission revoke hone par related collection stop karo aur dashboard mein status update karo.

4. Notification History Flow
User Android settings se notification access enable kare.
Supported notification events ko receive karo.
Event ID, package name, timestamp aur available notification metadata ko local queue mein store karo.
Notification data ko category aur date ke according filter karne ki facility do.
Duplicate events ko unique identifier ya deduplication logic se handle karo.
Internet unavailable hone par events pending rahen.
Internet available hone par authorized events backend par sync hon.
Admin dashboard par date-wise notification history display ho.
Sensitive notification content ko collect karne se pehle clear disclosure aur appropriate controls implement karo. Authentication codes, passwords aur other sensitive notification content ko exclude karna prefer karo.

5. Call History Flow
Call-log feature ki availability aur permission check karo.
Android version aur applicable distribution policies ke according supported call-log access implement karo.
Permitted records mein available fields jaise call type, timestamp, duration aur phone number handle karo.
Incremental synchronization use karo, jahan supported ho.
Records local queue mein save karo.
Successful server acknowledgment ke baad retention policy ke according local records clear karo.
Admin panel par date filter, call-type filter aur pagination provide karo.
Agar direct call-log access unavailable ho, to feature ko unavailable mark karo aur supported user-initiated import alternative provide karo. Call audio recording include mat karo.

6. App Usage Tracking Flow
User se Usage Access enable karvao.
Android UsageStatsManager se supported usage statistics retrieve karo.
Daily app usage duration, last-used information aur available summaries calculate karo.
Har sync cycle mein relevant time range ka data retrieve karo.
Duplicate records avoid karne ke liye device ID, package name aur time interval ke basis par stable record keys use karo.
Local queue se server par usage summaries sync karo.
Admin dashboard par daily usage, app-wise duration aur date-range reports display karo.
Sirf Android se available statistics show karo; doosre apps ka private internal data access karne ki koshish mat karo.

7. Gallery and File Management Flow
User Photo Picker ya Storage Access Framework se photos, videos ya documents select kare.
Selected items ka metadata local database mein store karo.
User ko selected items, total size aur sync status dikhayo.
Authorized files ko resumable ya retryable upload flow se server par bhejo.
Server successful upload ke baad file metadata aur storage reference MongoDB mein store kare.
Admin dashboard par permitted files ki list, preview aur download options provide karo.
Local files ko automatically delete mat karo. Deletion sirf explicit user configuration aur confirmed upload ke baad allowed ho.
Puri gallery ya unrestricted file system ko silently scan mat karo.

8. Local Data Queue and Automatic Synchronization
Implement a durable local-first synchronization system.

Har queued record mein appropriate fields hon:

recordId
deviceId
recordType
eventTimestamp
payload
syncStatus
retryCount
createdAt
lastAttemptAt
Possible sync statuses:

pending
uploading
synced
failed
Synchronization flow:

Eligible data event receive karo.
Record ko local persistent queue mein save karo.
Network availability check karo.
Internet unavailable hone par record pending rakho.
Internet available hone par pending batches backend ko bhejo.
Backend authentication, device ownership aur payload validate kare.
MongoDB mein idempotent upsert ya equivalent duplicate-safe write use karo.
Server successfully persist karne ke baad record-level acknowledgment return kare.
Client acknowledged records ko synced mark kare.
Configured retention policy ke according hi local copies delete karo.
Failed records ko exponential backoff ke saath retry karo.
Permanent failures ko error state mein rakho aur diagnostics provide karo.
Network connectivity ko server availability ka proof mat samjho. Actual request result aur server acknowledgment ke basis par status update karo.

Use paginated or bounded batches. Large gallery files ko normal JSON payload mein embed mat karo.

9. Automatic Background Sync
React Native mein existing background-task solution ko reuse karo.

Android par WorkManager-compatible scheduling ya existing maintained background-task library use karo.
Network constraint available hone par pending data synchronize karo.
App foreground mein aane par bhi pending sync check karo.
App startup par queue recovery perform karo.
Duplicate workers aur simultaneous upload conflicts prevent karo.
Reboot, process termination aur temporary network failures ke baad recover karne ka supported flow implement karo.
Battery optimization aur Android background restrictions ko respect karo.
User ko last sync time, pending record count aur failed record count dikhao.
Background tasks guaranteed real-time nahi hote. Har event ko instantly upload hone ka promise mat karo.

10. Optional Screen Sharing
Screen sharing ko normal data synchronization se alag feature rakho.

User admin request ya local action par screen-sharing request initiate kar sake.
Device B par Android MediaProjection consent dialog dikhaya jaye.
User consent ke baad hi sharing session start ho.
Active session ka clear indicator aur stop control ho.
Session end hone, permission revoke hone ya capture failure par sharing stop ho.
Admin dashboard par session status display ho.
Session start/stop events audit log mein store hon.
Mobile data enable hote hi screen capture automatically start mat karo. Android ki required consent aur foreground-service restrictions bypass mat karo.

11. Admin Dashboard Functionality
Existing admin screens mein following features implement karo:

Dashboard
Enrolled devices
Last-seen timestamp
Last successful sync
Pending synchronization count
Permission status
Recent synchronization errors
Device Details
Device metadata
Available feature status
Sync history
Permission health
Device unlink and revoke controls
Notification History
Date range
Package/app filter
Pagination
Supported notification metadata
Call History
Date range
Call type
Available authorized call-log fields
App Usage
Daily summaries
App-wise usage
Date-range reports
Files
Selected file list
File metadata
Upload status
Authorized preview/download
Har dashboard request authenticated backend API se data fetch kare. Data ko sirf local UI state ya mock arrays se render mat karo.

12. Backend API Integration
Existing Express routes aur authentication middleware reuse karo. Missing endpoints ko project ke existing conventions ke according add karo.

Suggested functionality:

Device registration and pairing
Device listing and details
Permission status updates
Notification batch synchronization
Call-log batch synchronization
App-usage synchronization
Selected-file upload initiation and completion
Sync acknowledgment and error reporting
Admin history queries with pagination
Device unlinking and revocation
Retention and deletion requests
Har endpoint par authenticated user, device ownership, payload validation, rate limits aur authorization enforce karo.

MongoDB indexes add karo jo account ID, device ID, event timestamp aur stable record ID ke common query patterns ko support karein.

13. Reliability and Security Rules
Existing authentication tokens aur authorization middleware reuse karo.
Sensitive data HTTPS se transmit karo.
Local queue mein unnecessary sensitive fields mat rakho.
Sensitive local data ko platform-supported secure storage/encryption se protect karo.
Server-side idempotency implement karo.
Upload confirmation ke bina queued records delete mat karo.
Device revocation ke baad future sync aur dashboard access reject karo.
Audit log mein authentication, pairing, export, deletion aur administrative actions record karo.
Configurable retention aur data deletion implement karo.
API errors mein secrets ya sensitive payloads log mat karo.
14. Implementation Instructions
Pehle existing repository inspect karo:

React Native navigation and state management
Existing permission modules
Current background task implementation
API service layer
Express routes and middleware
MongoDB models and indexes
Existing admin dashboard screens
Uske baad:

Existing functionality aur missing modules ki list banao.
Feature-wise implementation plan banao.
Ek module complete karke test karo.
Existing files ko unnecessarily replace mat karo.
Har new permission aur Android limitation document karo.
Offline sync, duplicate uploads, failed uploads aur permission revocation ke tests add karo.
End mein changed files, environment variables, API changes aur manual testing steps ki report do.
Sabse pehle device pairing, local queue, reliable sync acknowledgment aur admin dashboard integration implement karo. Uske baad notification, usage, call-log aur selected-file modules ko independently complete karo.